title: Sorting, lining up, and tidy programs
card: Chapter 16 | Sorting | Biggest first, and by what each works out to
say:
  Real programs sort things, line them up in columns, and grow into several scripts. Here are the words for that.
uncard

new: spending.fathom
type fast:
  a cost has:
    kind (text)
    amount (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to cost of, given kind (text) and amount (a number), returning a cost:
    conjure a cost as c
    set the kind of c to kind
    set the amount of c to amount
    return c
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    set costs to a list containing (cost of with ("food", 20.75), cost of with ("rent", 700), cost of with ("fun", 20))
    for each c in sorted costs by amount, biggest first:
      scrawl the kind of c padded to 8 letters, the amount of c
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: lines 15-17
say:
  Sorted costs by amount puts the smallest first. Adding biggest first turns it round. Padded to eight letters puts spaces after each kind, so the amounts line up in a column.
zoom: #output
wait
zoom: out

select: 16-16
type:
      scrawl the kind of c padded to 8 letters, the amount of c
    scrawl sorted a list containing ("Tomas", "Al", "Rex") by each n becomes the size of n
keys: enter
run
zoom: #output
say:
  Sorting can also go by anything worked out from each item. Here, by each n becomes the size of n: the shortest name first. Things that come out the same keep the order they had.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 16 | Text | Every alphabet
say:
  Text words count letters, not bytes, so accents, other alphabets and emoji all work the way they look.
uncard
new: letters.fathom
type fast:
  genesis:
    set word to "straße Ωμέγα 😀"
    scrawl upper case of word
    scrawl the size of word, " letters; the last is ", letter (the size of word) of word
    scrawl "ab" repeated 3 times
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: #output
say:
  Upper case changes every alphabet. A letter with no single capital, like this German one, stays as it is. The emoji counts as one letter, and repeated gives text that many times over.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 16 | Several scripts | Keeping a command to its own script
say:
  As a program grows into several scripts, two of them may want a helper with the same name. A command written privately is kept to its own script.
uncard
new: money.fathom
type fast:
  to tidy, privately, given amount (a number), returning text:
    return "$" plus (amount rounded to 2 decimal places)
  and the universe said i love you

  to price tag, given amount (a number), returning text:
    return "costs " plus tidy with amount
  and the universe said i love you
save
new: shop.fathom
type fast:
  use: money.fathom

  to tidy, given name (text), returning text:
    return trimmed name
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    scrawl tidy with "  tea  ", " ", price tag with 3.25
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: #output
say:
  Money's tidy is written privately, so only money dot fathom can use it, and the shop can have a tidy of its own. Without privately, Fathom would say there are two commands called tidy, and where each one is.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 16 | Files | Is it there?
say:
  Asking whether a file or a folder is there reads the same way for both.
uncard
new: saves.fathom
type fast:
  genesis:
    if folder "saves" exists:
      scrawl "found the saves"
    otherwise:
      make the folder "saves"
      scrawl "made the saves folder"
    scrawl file "saves/game.txt" exists
    scrawl extension of "saves/game.txt", " ", file name of "saves/game.txt"
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: #output
say:
  Folder saves exists is yes or no, like file exists. Extension of, and file name of, take a path apart.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 16 | Kinds | Parts only a kind's own commands can touch
say:
  A part written hidden can only be used by the commands for that kind of thing. Everywhere else, it is a mistake to reach in and change it.
uncard
new: bank.fathom
type fast:
  an account has:
    balance (a number, hidden)
  and the universe said i love you

  a savings account is a kind of account that has:
    rate (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to pay in, for an account, given amount (a number):
    if amount falls below 0: raise an error with "pay in more than nothing"
    set the balance of account to the balance of account plus amount
  and the universe said i love you

  to balance now, for an account, returning a number:
    return the balance of account
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    conjure a savings account as mine
    pay in with (mine, 50)
    scrawl balance now mine
    scrawl mine is an account, " ", mine is a savings account
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: #output
say:
  Only pay in can change the balance, so it can't go wrong from outside. And is a asks what kind of thing something really is: a savings account is an account too.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 16 | The web | A server that says how it was asked
say:
  A web server's answer command can see how it was asked, with the web way, and say a page isn't there with a status.
uncard
new: tiny server.fathom
type fast:
  use: server
  use: web

  to answer, given address (text), returning text:
    if address is not "/":
      answer with the status 404
      return "no such page"
    return "you asked with " plus the web way
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    meanwhile serve the web with (8790, the command answer)
    wait 0.5
    scrawl ask the web with ("http://127.0.0.1:8790/", "POST", "hi"), ", status ", the last web status
    scrawl ask the web with ("http://127.0.0.1:8790/nope", "GET"), ", status ", the last web status
    end the program with 0
  and the universe said i love you
run
zoom: #output
say:
  The program serves the web alongside, then asks itself twice. The first answer knows it was a POST. The second page isn't there, so it comes back with status four oh four.
wait
zoom: out
